{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792774368,"nonce":"qBYpQlRBSE9fxb6oDXiblVK1n0k=","title":"Text measurement was not cached: the first layout of 900 text nodes took 70 to 90 seconds","message":"Found while taking the per-node heap census (d106687). A column of 300 rows, each a flex row holding two texts, took 67 to 89 s in its first computeLayout; 1,200 rows 123 s. A native sample showed blinc_layout's FontTextMeasurer shaping the text with rustybuzz on every measure, and taffy measuring each text several times per layout; it also always laid a single-line version out first, which only the min-content and max-content probes use.\n\n**Fix**\n\nA measurement cache in FontTextMeasurer, by text, face, size, line height, letter spacing and width, and the single-line layout made lazily. With it the same scene lays out in 36 ms at 300 rows and 145 ms at 1,200. Blinc commit c62c975c on branch layout-measure-cache, handed to blinc-16 to land; ashui then bumps its lock, as for the FxHash change (3ec0b2c).","files":null}]}